{
  "abstract": "An isogeny between elliptic curves induced by rational Diophantine triples need not transport their Diophantine entries. Rational marked normalization, recovery of individual square roots, and compatibility between additional entries are separate requirements. We give explicit formulas that retain these requirements for isogenies of degrees two and three. For degree two, the map preserves every anchor edge and every edge from an extender to an anchor. Its remaining mutual-edge condition is an exact square defect involving the regular-quintuple polynomial; in particular, regular quintuples transport on the stated open chart. An elliptic coset supplies infinitely many admissible source triples, and an exact rational source/target quintuple verifies all twenty square witnesses. The resulting classical triple family is identified rather than claimed as new. For degree three, we provide a conditional individual-root decoder and rationally parametrize the division-polynomial discriminant surface of regular source triples. This chart includes rational cyclic kernels with quadratic nonidentity points, which are omitted by a rational-torsion parametrization. On the latter, more restrictive subfamily, the full normalization problem has an explicit genus-five quotient and a necessary cubic rational-root lift. Generically the genus-thirteen normalization curve is an unramified cyclic triple cover of this quotient. Standard cyclic-isogeny restrictions explain which degrees and regular exterior configurations the interface can support. Standalone symbolic certificates and exact controls accompany the formulas. No rational septuple, new sextuple family, or nondegenerate normalized degree-three example is asserted.",
